# Add Condition Field to Custom Merchandise

Add a "Condition" field (e.g., Brand New, Used, Like New) to the custom merchandise catalog to provide clearer product information to customers.

## Proposed Changes

### Database & Model

#### [MODIFY] [Custom_model.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/models/Custom_model.php)
- Add a "self-healing" `ALTER TABLE` statement in the constructor to ensure the `product_condition` column exists in the `custom_products` table if it doesn't already.

### Admin Controller & Logic

#### [MODIFY] [Admin.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Admin.php)
- Update the `save_custom()` method to capture and save the `product_condition` from the form POST data.
- **[NEW]** Implement the `edit_custom($id)` method to load a product for editing (this appears to be missing in the current controller).
- **[NEW]** Implement the `update_custom()` method to process edits, including the new condition field.

### Admin Views

#### [MODIFY] [add_custom.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/views/admin/add_custom.php)
- Add a "Product Condition" dropdown selection (options: Brand New, Like New, Lightly Used, Well Used).

#### [NEW] [edit_custom.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/views/admin/edit_custom.php)
- Create a dedicated edit page for custom products (based on the `add_custom.php` layout) that includes the new condition field.

### Storefront View

#### [MODIFY] [view_custom_product.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/views/store/view_custom_product.php)
- Update the "Product Specifications" section to display the actual `product_condition` from the database instead of the hardcoded "Brand New" placeholder.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. Log in as Admin.
2. Go to "Add Custom Merchandise".
3. Verify the "Condition" dropdown is present.
4. Add a product with "Used" condition.
5. Go to the public store and view the product.
6. Verify the specs show "Used" instead of "Brand New".
7. Click "Edit Details" in the admin inventory.
8. Change the condition to "Brand New" and save.
9. Verify the change reflected in the store.
